From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 23:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: cedrus: encode H.264 pictures up to 4096x4096

The H616 datasheet gives the encoder 4096x4096. Pictures wider than 2048
pixels keep the context of a macroblock row in the external line buffer
of 0xbc4 instead of the engine's own memory; the vendor library of the
T527 sizes it at 8 bytes per luma column and sets no other register for
them, the mode register's picture width bits being the decoder's (the
vendor libraries set them on the decode path only). Every picture
already gets a line buffer of twice that size, so lift the limit from
2048x2048 to 4096x4096. The other register fields hold these sizes (the
input stage size in units of 8 pixels in 11 bits, the stride in
macroblocks divided by 48 in 4 bits).

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_enc.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_enc.c
@@ -31,16 +31,17 @@
 #include "cedrus_video.h"
 
 /*
- * Pictures wider than 2048 pixels need the external deblocking line buffer
- * (VE_ENC_AVC_DEBLK_ADDR) that the vendor library programs on the T527;
- * it is not known for the H616 yet, so the encoder stops at 2048.
+ * Up to 4096x4096, the encoder's limit in the H616 datasheet. Pictures
+ * wider than 2048 pixels keep the context of a macroblock row in the
+ * external line buffer (VE_ENC_AVC_DEBLK_ADDR, 8 bytes per luma column in
+ * the vendor library of the T527), which every picture gets.
  */
 static const struct v4l2_frmsize_stepwise cedrus_enc_frmsize = {
 	.min_width	= 16,
-	.max_width	= 2048,
+	.max_width	= 4096,
 	.step_width	= 2,
 	.min_height	= 16,
-	.max_height	= 2048,
+	.max_height	= 4096,
 	.step_height	= 2,
 };
 
